<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bokar Saada</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bokar <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saada">Saada</a> was almamy of Bundu, the Muslim clerical state on the upper <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/senegal">Senegal</a>, in the second half of the 19th century. Brought to power with French support, he sided with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> against Umar Tall and other rivals and used French backing to strengthen his rule. His alliance prepared the way for the French <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protectorate">protectorate</a> over Bundu in the 1880s.</p></div>
